# Natural statement: for real a and b, a < b implies a <= b.
#
# Before this MVP, the compiler emitted only Litex's canonical wrapper theorem
# for this source. There was no generated native-real theorem that an ordinary
# Mathlib file could import and use.
#
# Now the same typed verifier evidence produces both the canonical theorem and
# a `Native` theorem over Mathlib's `Real`. The native proof replays the checked
# strict-to-weak order rule through reviewed Litex order bridges.
#
# Boundary: this MVP recognizes exactly two direct R binders with the premise
# `a < b`, conclusion `a <= b`, and allowlisted strict-to-weak order evidence.
# Other theorem shapes remain canonical-only and fail closed at this export
# layer. No Same-to-equality shortcut, axiom, `sorry`, or `admit` is introduced.
#
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -runner -f showcases/litex_to_mathlib_pipeline/main.lit
# target/release/stmt_result_to_lean_compiler compile showcases/litex_to_mathlib_pipeline/main.lit showcases/litex_to_mathlib_pipeline/LitexToMathlibPipelineGenerated.lean
# (cd lean && lake build LitexToMathlibPipeline)

thm litex_real_lt_to_le:
    ? forall a, b R:
        a < b
        =>:
            a <= b
